m 65 G\");\n    it.todo(\"should quote 4 runes without block discount -- premium 105 G\");\n    it.todo(\"should quote 7 runes without block discount -- premium 180 G\");\n    it.todo(\"should quote 2 runes + 1 moonstone as different types -- premium 80 G\");\n    it.todo(\"should quote 3 runes + 3 moonstones as two blocks -- premium 125 G\");\n    it.todo(\"should apply cursed surcharge to cursed sword -- premium 160 G before fee\");\n    it.todo(\"should apply high-enchantment surcharge at enchantment 5 -- premium 135 G\");\n    it.todo(\"should apply loyalty discount at exactly 2 years -- premium 84 G\");\n    it.todo(\"should apply first-insurance surcharge and follow-up discount on second contract\");\n    it.todo(\"should handle newcomer with cursed sword -- premium 165 G\");\n    it.todo(\"should handle long-standing customer second contract with cursed enchanted sword -- premium 160 G\");\n    it.todo(\"should sum insurance values for multiple items of same type -- two swords sum 2000 G\");\n    it.todo(\"should quote a mixed policy with item-specific and policy-wide modifiers\");\n    it.todo(\"should reject unknown item type in quote\");\n  });\n\n  describe(\"claim\", () => {\n    it.todo(\"should pay regular sword damage 500 G minus deductible -- payout 400 G\");\n    it.todo(\"should pay rune damage 200 G minus deductible -- payout 100 G\");\n    it.todo(\"should apply high-enchantment clause to dragon-material sword enchantment 8 -- payout 400 G\");\n    it.todo(\"should apply dragon-material clause to enchantment 5 sword -- payout 700 G\");\n    it.todo(\"should apply high-enchantment clause to steel sword enchantment 9 -- payout 400 G\");\n    it.todo(\"should apply high-enchantment clause over dragon material when both apply -- payout 400 G\");\n    it.todo(\"should apply deductible per damaged item in multi-item incident\");\n    it.todo(\"should cap total payout at twice the insurance sum\");\n    it.todo(\"should exhaust cap across successive claims\");\n    it.todo(\"should reject claim for item not in policy\");\n    it.todo(\"should reject claim with negative damage amount\");\n    it.todo(\"should reject claim with more damages of a type than policy covers\");\n  });\n\n  describe(\"processScenario\", () => {\n    it.todo(\"should process quote then claim from schema example\");\n  });\n});\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784969991964},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.ls:2","toolName":"ls","content":[{"type":"text","text":".pi/\nAGENTS.md\neslint.config.mjs\nmetrics.json\nnode_modules/\npackage.json\npnpm-lock.yaml\nprompt.md\nrun.log\nsrc/\ntsconfig.json\nvitest.config.ts"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784969991964},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"We need refactor claim-office.ts. Current implementation has quote uses only first item base premium. There are placeholder claim and processScenario. Passing tests: 5 quote tests. Need keep all tests green. We must attempt at least one refactoring. Evaluate naming first. Potential improvements: BASE_PREMIUMS typed Record<string, number>, but can restrict to known item types maybe union type ItemType to improve type safety and reveal intent. quote function name fits. It currently ignores customer; fine. Could extract `calculateBasePremium` helper? Maybe not. Could define InsuredItem type with better names? `type` is string; can be union. However given future tests include runes, moonstones etc unknown; union could be ItemType = 'sword' | 'amulet' | 'staff' | 'potion' | 'rune' | 'moonstone' maybe. But we don't know full spec. It might be okay. But we must keep tests green. The mandatory refactoring: attempt at least one improvement. We can refactor by introducing an `ItemType` union and using it for BASE_PREMIUMS keys and InsuredItem.type. This reveals intent and improves type safety. Need ensure TypeScript compiles and tests pass.\n\nNeed calculate APP mass before and after. Need run tests before. Let's run tests."