 precise term. \"Group\" was too generic and hid the block-discount concept.\n- **`quote`**: name still fits — it produces a premium quote.\n- **`claim` / `processScenario`**: still match their intended purpose.\n\n### Structural Improvements\n\nExtracted three single-responsibility helpers from `quote` so it reads as a high-level recipe:\n\n1. **`basePremiumFor(items)`** — calculates policy base premium from item groups.\n2. **`cursedSurchargeFor(items)`** — calculates per-item cursed surcharge.\n3. **`firstInsuranceSurchargeFor(basePremium, contractIndex)`** — calculates the first-insurance surcharge.\n\n`quote` now composes these named operations instead of mixing loops, conditionals, and arithmetic inline.\n\n### Simple Design Assessment\n\n| Rule | Assessment |\n|------|------------|\n| **1. Tests Pass** | All 12 passing tests remain green after refactoring. |\n| **2. Reveals Intent** | Improved — `quote` now expresses *what* is being summed; helper names explain *why*. |\n| **3. No Duplication** | `premiumForGroup` is reused for base premium and cursed surcharge; no new duplication introduced. |\n| **4. Fewest Elements** | Trade-off accepted: three new functions add elements but dramatically improve readability of `quote`. |\n\n### APP Mass Calculation\n\n**Current Code Mass** (before):\n\n```\nConstants:  18  × 1  = 18\nBindings:   32  × 1  = 32\nInvocations: 22  × 2  = 44\nConditionals: 4  × 4  = 16\nLoops:       3  × 5  = 15\nAssignments: 2  × 6  = 12\n-----------------------------\nTotal Mass: 137\n```\n\n**Refactored Code Mass** (after):\n\n```\nConstants:  21  × 1  = 21\nBindings:   38  × 1  = 38\nInvocations: 25  × 2  = 50\nConditionals: 4  × 4  = 16\nLoops:       3  × 5  = 15\nAssignments: 2  × 6  = 12\n-----------------------------\nTotal Mass: 152\n```\n\n**Mass Change**: `137 → 152` (+15)\n\n### Decision Rationale\n\nMass increased slightly because extracting helpers adds bindings and invocations. Per Rule 2, clarity takes priority over raw mass. The `quote` function now clearly decomposes into:\n\n```\nprocessing fee + base premium + cursed surcharge + first-insurance surcharge\n```\n\nwhich directly mirrors how the specification and tests describe the quote calculation. The helper functions each have a single reason to change, making future tests (loyalty discount, enchantment surcharge, etc.) easier to slot in without disturbing existing logic.\n\n### Verification\n\n```\n✓ src/claim-office.spec.ts  (33 tests | 21 skipped)\nTest Files  1 passed (1)\nTests  12 passed | 21 todo (33)\n```"}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_08-56-23_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_kimi-k2-7/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 12\nRecent Green phase: applied cursed surcharge, first-insurance surcharge, and premium rounding\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 12\nRecent Green phase: applied cursed surcharge, first-insurance surcharge, and premium rounding\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784970192089},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to refactor the implementation in `src/claim-office.ts` while keeping all tests in `src/claim-office.spec.ts` green. I need to follow the refactoring guidelines carefully.\n\nLet me start by reading the test file and implementation file to understand what we're working with.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.read:0","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/cla