ment = 30% of 100 = 30\n- first insurance = 10% of 100 = 10\n- fee = 5\n- total = 145\n\nWait, the test description says premium 135 G. That doesn't match. Let me re-read: \"should apply high-enchantment surcharge at enchantment 5 -- premium 135 G\". Hmm. Maybe it's an amulet? Amulet base 60 + high enchantment 18 + first insurance 6 + fee 5 = 89. Not 135.\n\nMaybe 135 is before fee? Sword: 100 + 30 + 10 = 140 before fee. Not 135.\n\nMaybe the test is meant to be a high-enchantment sword at contractIndex 1 (follow-up discount)? 100 + 30 - 15 + 10 + 5 = 130. Not 135.\n\nHmm. Maybe the description is wrong. Let me think. For a sword enchantment 5, cursed false, new customer, first contract:\n100 + 30 + 10 + 5 = 145.\n\nIf contractIndex 1 (follow-up): 100 + 30 - 15 + 10 + 5 = 130.\n\nIf customer 2 years (loyalty): 100 + 30 - 20 + 10 + 5 = 125.\n\nIf both loyalty and follow-up: 100 + 30 - 20 - 15 + 10 + 5 = 110.\n\nNone give 135.\n\nMaybe the test is for high enchantment on a non-sword? Staff base 80 + 24 + 8 + 5 = 117. Amulet 60 + 18 + 6 + 5 = 89. Potion 40 + 12 + 4 + 5 = 61.\n\nMaybe \"premium 135 G\" refers to before fee? Sword before fee: 140. Staff before fee: 112. Amulet before fee: 84.\n\nWait, maybe the test is for a cursed high-enchantment sword with some discounts? Cursed sword enchantment 5, new customer, first contract: 100 + 50 + 30 + 10 + 5 = 195. Not 135.\n\nMaybe the original test list value was wrong. I should make the test match the actual expected value. Since the description says \"high-enchantment surcharge at enchantment 5\", I'll test a sword with enchantment 5 and expect 145 (final premium) or maybe just test that the high enchantment surcharge is applied and check a value.\n\nActually, to keep it simple, let me make the test for a sword enchantment 5 and expect 145. I'll update the description. The value 135 in my test list was probably an error.\n\nWait, actually maybe 135 is base premium + high enchantment + fee, without first insurance? 100 + 