ontent":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good. Proceed to next Red phase.\n\n## Red -- Test 14: Loyalty discount at exactly 2 years → premium 84 G\n\nLoyalty discount: 20% of policy base. Test description says premium 84 G. Let's calculate for a single sword, new contract (first insurance), customer 2 years:\n- base 100\n- first insurance 10\n- loyalty -20\n- fee 5\n- total = 95\n\nNot 84. For amulet: 60 + 6 - 12 + 5 = 59. Staff: 80 + 8 - 16 + 5 = 77. Potion: 40 + 4 - 8 + 5 = 41.\n\nMaybe 84 is for a sword with follow-up discount? 100 + 10 - 15 - 20 + 5 = 80.\n\nMaybe 84 is for an amulet with follow-up? 60 + 6 - 12 - 15 + 5 = 44.\n\nHmm. What item gives 84? \n- 2 runes: base 50 + first ins 5 - loyalty 10 + fee 5 = 50. No.\n- 3 runes block: 60 + 6 - 12 + 5 = 59.\n- 4 runes: 100 + 10 - 20 + 5 = 95.\n- 2 runes + 1 moonstone: 75 + 7.5 - 15 + 5 = 72.5 → 73.\n\nMaybe 84 is the value before fee? Sword with loyalty, before fee: 100 + 10 - 20 = 90. Amulet: 60 + 6 - 12 = 54.\n\nI think 84 in my test list was an arbitrary/incorrect value. Let me just test loyalty discount with a simple case. For a single sword, customer 2 years, first contract: expected 95. I'll update the test.\n\nActually, the spec example says \"customer with exactly 2 years with MHPCO → loyalty discount applies\". It doesn't give a specific premium. So I can choose any item. Let me use sword and expect 95.\n\nLet me activate.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.edit:85","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_08-56-23_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_kimi-k2-7/src/claim-office.spec.ts","edits":[{"oldText":"    it.todo(\"should apply loyalty discount at exactly 2 years -- premium 84 G\");","newText":"    it(\"should apply loyalty discount at exactly 2 years -- premium 95 G\", () => {\n      const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 2 };\n      const items = [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment