unt include `itemSurchargesFor` binding? Yes. Final rename doesn't change mass. Good.\n\nNow need produce final response. But this is a subagent task; the main agent expects summary. We should output the refactoring report. It should be concise but include naming evaluation, mass, decisions, tests. The instructions in system prompt want documentation. We can format.\n\nNeed ensure we mention we attempted multiple refactorings. We should mention:\n- Naming: `itemSurchargesFor` renamed to `totalItemSurchargeFor` (reveals it returns total, not list).\n- Grouped `FOLLOW_UP_DISCOUNT_RATE` with contract constants.\n- Simplified `contractModifierFor` to express modifier as basePremium * selected signed rate, removing duplicated multiplication.\n- Inlined `total` variable in `quote`, returning `Math.ceil(...)` directly.\n- Replaced imperative loop/accumulator in `basePremiumFor` with functional `Array.from(...).reduce(...)`, removing mutable `let` and `+=`.\n\nTests all green. Mass 166 -> 164. We can note small mass change but main wins are removal of mutable accumulator and naming clarity. Rule 2 clarity maintained.\n\nHowever, is the mass reduction of 2 meaningful? It's small. We should not overstate. We can mention APP mass decreased modestly, but primary improvement is intent and removal of mutable state. Since instructions say lower mass = better generally. We measured.\n\nShould we consider that we could have done a bigger mass reduction? Maybe but we kept clarity. We can note other candidates considered but not applied to preserve clarity. But not necessary.\n\nNeed final answer.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Refactoring complete.\n\n### Naming Evaluation (Rule 2 first)\n- `itemSurchargesFor(items)` returned a **single total number**, but the name read like it returned a collection.  \n  **Decision:** Renamed to `totalItemSurchargeFor(items)` to reveal intent.\n- `contractModifierFor` computed the same `basePremium * …` expression twice.  \n  **Decision:** Consolidated to one multiplication with a selected signed rate.\n- `FOLLOW_UP_DISCOUNT_RATE` was separated from the other contract-rate constants.  \n  **Decision:** Moved it next to `FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE`.\n\n### APP Mass Calculation\nScope: `src/claim-office.ts`\n\n**Before refactoring:**\n```\nConstants:   30\nBindings:    57\nInvocations: 17\nConditionals: 6\nLoops:        3\nAssignments:  1\nTotal Mass: 166\n```\n\n**After refactoring:**\n```\nConstants:   30\nBindings:    57\nInvocations: 19\nConditionals: 6\nLoops:        3\nAssignments:  0\nTotal Mass: 164\n```\n\nMass change: **166 → 164**  \nThe main gain is the removal of the mutable accumulator/assignment in `basePremiumFor`.\n\n### Refactorings Applied\n1. **Grouped constants** – moved `FOLLOW_UP_DISCOUNT_RATE` with contract-rate constants.\n2. **Renamed** `itemSurchargesFor` → `totalItemSurchargeFor` for clearer intent.\n3. **Simplified `contractModifierFor`** to a single multiplication with a selected signed rate.\n4. **Inlined the `total` variable** in `quote`, returning `Math.ceil(...)` directly.\n5. **Replaced imperative loop in `basePremiumFor`** with `Array.from(groups).reduce(...)`, eliminating the mutable `let` and `+=`.\n\n### Tests\n```\nTest Files  1 passed (1)\nTests  15 passed | 18 todo (33)\n```\n\nAll tests remain green."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":232,"output":996,"cacheRead":25984,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":566,"totalTokens":27212,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1784970530638,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-8e28535a-3fe2-4a10-b3c0-a595a323f87b","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"}],"stderr":"","usage":{"input":8375,"output":13650,"cacheRead":467328,"cacheWrite":0,"cost":0,"contextTokens":27212,"turns":25},"model":"requesty/tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","stopReason":"stop"}]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1784970535356},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Read current file.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.read:96","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_08-56-23_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_kimi-k2-7/src/claim-office.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":500,"output":69,"cacheRead":65984,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":5,"totalTokens":66553,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784970535367,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-3e6e1118-85f1-4f68-bb6d-7ded42382875","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.read:96","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"type InsuredItem = {\n  type: string;\n  material: string;\n  enchantment: number;\n  cursed: boolean;\n};\n\ntype Customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: number };\n\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM = 60;\n\nconst CURSED_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.5;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD = 5;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.3;\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.1;\nconst FOLLOW_UP_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.15;\nconst LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.2;\n\nconst BASE_PREMIUMS: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n  rune: 25,\n  moonstone: 25,\n};\n\nconst COMPONENT_TYPES = new Set([\"rune\", \"moonstone\"]);\n\nconst componentBlockPremium = (count: number, unitPremium: number): number =>\n  count === COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE ? COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM : count * unitPremium;\n\nconst unitPremiumFor = (type: string): number => BASE_PREMIUMS[type] ?? 0;\n\nconst premiumForGroup = (type: string, count: number): number => {\n  const unitPremium = unitPremiumFor(type);\n  return COMPONENT_TYPES.has(type)\n    ? componentBlockPremium(count, unitPremium)\n    : count * unitPremium;\n};\n\nconst countByType = (items: InsuredItem[]): Map<string, number> => {\n  const counts = new Map<string, number>();\n  for (const item of items) {\n    counts.set(item.type, (counts.get(item.type) ?? 0) + 1);\n  }\n  return counts;\n};\n\nconst basePremiumFor = (items: InsuredItem[]): number => {\n  const groups = countByType(items);\n  return Array.from(groups).reduce(\n    (total, [type, count]) => total + premiumForGroup(type, count),\n    0,\n  );\n};\n\nconst itemSurchargeFor = (item: InsuredItem): number => {\n  const base = unitPremiumFor(item.type);\n  const cursedSurcharge = item.cursed ? base * CURSED_SURCHARGE_RATE : 0;\n  const enchantmentSurcharge =\n    item.enchantment >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD\n      ? base * HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE\n      : 0;\n  return cursedSurcharge + enchantmentSurcharge;\n};\n\nconst totalItemSurchargeFor = (items: InsuredItem[]): number =>\n  items.reduce((total, item) => total + itemSurchargeFor(item), 0);\n\nconst contractModifierFor = (\n  basePremium: number,\n  contractIndex: number,\n): number =>\n  basePremium *\n  (contractIndex === 0\n    ? FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE\n    : -FOLLOW_UP_DISCOUNT_RATE);\n\nconst loyaltyDiscountFor = (customer: Customer, basePremium: number): number =>\n  customer.yearsWithMHPCO >= 2 ? basePremium * LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE : 0;\n\nexport const quote = (\n  customer: Customer,\n  items: InsuredItem[],\n  contractIndex: number = 0,\n): number => {\n  const policyBasePremium = basePremiumFor(items);\n  const itemSurcharges = totalItemSurchargeFor(items);\n  const contractModifier = contractModifierFor(policyBasePremium, contractIndex);\n  const loyaltyDiscount = loyaltyDiscountFor(customer, policyBasePremium);\n  return Math.ceil(\n    PROCESSING_FEE +\n      policyBasePremium +\n      itemSurcharges +\n      contractModifier -\n      loyaltyDiscount,\n  );\n};\n\nexport const claim = (\n  policy: unknown,\n  incident: unknown,\n): { payout: number; remainingCap: number } => ({ payout: 0, remainingCap: 0 });\n\nexport const processScenario = (scenario: unknown): unknown => undefined;\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784970536696},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Proceed to next Red phase.\n\n## Red -- Test 16: Newcomer with cursed sword → premium 165 G\n\nThis should pass now. Let me activate.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.edit:97","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_08-56-23_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_kimi-k2-7/src/claim-office.spec.ts","edits":[{"oldText":"    it.todo(\"should handle newcomer with cursed sword -- premium 165 G\");","newText":"    it(\"should handle newcomer with cursed sword -- premium 165 G\", () => {\n      const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n      const items = [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: true }];\n      expect(quote(customer, items, 0)).toBe(165);\n    });"}]}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":932,"output":221,"cacheRead":66496,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":36,"totalTokens":67649,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784970536699,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-43de6da2-0dcd-432f-8f2c-47a2821fe389","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.edit:97","toolName":"edit","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully replaced 1 block(s) in /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_08-56-23_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_kimi-k2-7/src/claim-office.spec.ts."}],"details":{"diff":"     ...\n 104       const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n 105       const items = [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false }];\n 106       expect(quote(customer, items, 1)).