he duplicated `count * unitPremium` fallback path that existed in both `componentBlockPremium` and `premiumForGroup`.\n\n**APP Mass Calculation** (scope: `componentBlockPremium` + `premiumForGroup` region)\n\nCounting method:\n- Constants: literal values\n- Bindings: parameters and local variables (per declaration, not per use)\n- Invocations: function/method calls\n- Conditionals: `if` / ternary / `switch`\n- Loops: iteration constructs\n- Assignments: reassignments/mutations only\n\n*Before refactor:*\n```ts\nconst componentBlockPremium = (count: number, unitPremium: number): number =>\n  count === COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE ? COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM : count * unitPremium;\n\nconst premiumForGroup = (type: string, count: number): number => {\n  const unitPremium = unitPremiumFor(type);\n  return COMPONENT_TYPES.has(type)\n    ? componentBlockPremium(count, unitPremium)\n    : count * unitPremium;\n};\n```\n- Bindings: 5 (`count`, `unitPremium`, `type`, `count`, `unitPremium`)\n- Invocations: 3 (`has`, `componentBlockPremium`, `unitPremiumFor`) → 6\n- Conditionals: 2 (two ternaries) → 8\n- Constants: 0\n- Loops: 0\n- Assignments: 0\n- **Total Mass: 19**\n\n*After refactor:*\n```ts\nconst premiumForGroup = (type: string, count: number): number => {\n  const unitPremium = unitPremiumFor(type);\n  if (COMPONENT_TYPES.has(type) && count === COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE) {\n    return COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM;\n  }\n  return count * unitPremium;\n};\n```\n- Bindings: 3 (`type`, `count`, `unitPremium`)\n- Invocations: 2 (`unitPremiumFor`, `has`) → 4\n- Conditionals: 1 (`if`) → 4\n- Constants: 0\n- Loops: 0\n- Assignments: 0\n- **Total Mass: 11**\n\n**Mass Change:** 19 → 11 (Δ −8)\n\n**Simple Design Rules Check**\n1. **Tests pass:** `pnpm test` → 17 passing, 16 todo.\n2. **Reveals intent:** Removed the misleading `componentBlockPremium`; the block-discount rule is now explicit inside `premiumForGroup`.\n3. **No duplication:** The fallback `count * unitPremium` now appears only once.\n4. **Fewest elements:** One helper function removed.\n\n**Tests:** All passing."}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_08-56-23_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_kimi-k2-7/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 17\nRecent Green phase: separated first-insurance surcharge (always applied) and follow-up discount (applied on later contracts)\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 17\nRecent Green phase: separated first-insurance surcharge (always applied) and follow-up discount (applied on later contracts)\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784970555674},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"We are a refactoring subagent. We have a task: refactor implementation in src/claim-office.ts while keeping tests in src/claim-office.spec.ts green. Need to apply at least one refactoring, evaluate naming first, calculate APP mass before/after, document decisions.\n\nWe need to read files, run tests, decide refactoring. Need to use tools. We have no subagent tool (this agent context). We'll use bash, read, edit.\n\nFirst, read current implementation and tests.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.read:0","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.read:1","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":72,"output":137,"cacheRead":6016,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":99,"totalTokens":6225,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784970555694,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-adf4d400-965a-4cd1-ab01-026c17a66966","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.read:0","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"type InsuredItem = {\n  type: string;\n  material: string;\n  enchantment: number;\n  cursed: boolean;\n};\n\ntype Customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: number };\n\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM = 60;\n\nconst CURSED_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.5;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD = 5;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.3;\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.1;\nconst FOLLOW_UP_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.15;\nconst LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.2;\n\nconst BASE_PREMIUMS: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n  rune: 25,\n  moonstone: 25,\n};\n\nconst COMPONENT_TYPES = new Set([\"rune\", \"moonstone\"]);\n\nconst componentBlockPremium = (count: number, unitPremium: number): number =>\n  count === COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE ? COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM : count * unitPremium;\n\nconst unitPremiumFor = (type: string): number => BASE_PREMIUMS[type] ?? 0;\n\nconst premiumForGroup = (type: string, count: number): number => {\n  const unitPremium = unitPremiumFor(type);\n  return COMPONENT_TYPES.has(type)\n    ? componentBlockPremium(count, unitPremium)\n    : count * unitPremium;\n};\n\nconst countByType = (items: InsuredItem[]): Map<string, number> => {\n  const counts = new Map<string, number>();\n  for (const item of items) {\n    counts.set(item.type, (counts.get(item.type) ?? 0) + 1);\n  }\n  return counts;\n};\n\nconst basePremiumFor = (items: InsuredItem[]): number => {\n  const groups = countByType(items);\n  return Array.from(groups).reduce(\n    (total, [type, count]) => total + premiumForGroup(type, count),\n    0,\n  );\n};\n\nconst itemSurchargeFor = (item: InsuredItem): number => {\n  const base = unitPremiumFor(item.type);\n  const cursedSurcharge = item.cursed ? base * CURSED_SURCHARGE_RATE : 0;\n  const enchantmentSurcharge =\n    item.enchantment >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD\n      ? base * HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE\n      : 0;\n  return cursedSurcharge + enchantmentSurcharge;\n};\n\nconst totalItemSurchargeFor = (items: InsuredItem[]): number =>\n  items.reduce((total, item) => total + itemSurchargeFor(item), 0);\n\nconst firstInsuranceSurchargeFor = (basePremium: number): number =>\n  basePremium * FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE;\n\nconst followUpDiscountFor = (\n  basePremium: number,\n  contractIndex: number,\n): number =>\n  contractIndex > 0 ? basePremium * FOLLOW_UP_DISCOUNT_RATE : 0;\n\nconst loyaltyDiscountFor = (customer: Customer, basePremium: number): number =>\n  customer.yearsWithMHPCO >= 2 ? basePremium * LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE : 0;\n\nexport const quote = (\n  customer: Customer,\n  items: InsuredItem[],\n  contractIndex: number = 0,\n): number => {\n  const policyBasePremium = basePremiumFor(items);\n  const itemSurcharges = totalItemSurchargeFor(items);\n  const firstInsuranceSurcharge = firstInsuranceSurchargeFor(policyBasePremium);\n  const followUpDiscount = followUpDiscountFor(\n    policyBasePremium,\n    contractIndex,\n  );\n  const loyaltyDiscount = loyaltyDiscountFor(customer, policyBasePremium);\n  return Math.ceil(\n    PROCESSING_FEE +\n      policyBasePremium +\n      itemSurcharges +\n      firstInsuranceSurcharge -\n      followUpDiscount -\n      loyaltyDiscount,\n  );\n};\n\nexport const claim = (\n  policy: unknown,\n  incident: unknown,\n): { payout: number; remainingCap: number } => ({ payout: 0, remainingCap: 0 });\n\nexport const processScenario = (scenario: unknown): unknown => undefined;\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784970557089},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.read:1","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { quote, claim, processScenario } from \"./claim-office.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"MHPCO Claim Office\", () => {\n  describe(\"quote\", () => {\n    it(\"should return premium 5 G for empty item list -- only processing fee\", () => {\n      const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n      expect(quote(customer, [])).toBe(5);\n    });\n    it(\"should quote a single sword -- premium 115 G\", () => {\n      const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n      const items = [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false }];\n      expect(quote(customer, items, 0)).toBe(115);\n    });\n    it(\"should quote a single amulet -- premium 71 G\", () => {\n      const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n      const items = [{ type: \"amulet\", material: \"silver\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false }];\n      expect(quote(customer, items, 0)).toBe(71);\n    });\n    it(\"should quote a single staff -- premium 93 G\", () => {\n      const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n      const items = [{ type: \"staff\", material: \"wood\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false }];\n      expect(quote(customer, items, 0)).toBe(93);\n    });\n    it(\"should quote a single potion -- premium 49 G\", () => {\n      const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n      const items = [{ type: \"potion\", material: \"glass\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false }];\n      expect(quote(customer, items, 0)).toBe(49);\n    });\n    it(\"should quote 2 runes without block discount -- premium 60 G\", () => {\n      const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n      const items = [\n        { type: \"rune\", material: \"stone\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false },\n        { type: \"rune\", material: \"stone\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false },\n      ];\n      expect(quote(customer, items, 0)).toBe(60);\n    });\n    it(\"should quote 3 runes with block discount -- premium 71 G\", () => {\n      const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n      const items = [\n        { type: \"rune\", material: \"stone\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false },\n        { type: \"rune\", material: \"stone\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false },\n        { type: \"rune\", material: \"stone\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false },\n      ];\n      expect(quote(customer, items, 0)).toBe(71);\n    });\n    it(\"should quote 4 runes without block discount -- premium 115 G\", () => {\n      const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n      const items = [\n        { type: \"rune\", material: \"stone\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false },\n        { type: \"rune\", material: \"stone\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false },\n        { type: \"rune\", material: \"stone\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false },\n        { type: \"rune\", material: \"stone\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false },\n      ];\n      expect(quote(customer, items, 0)).toBe(115);\n    });\n    it(\"should quote 7 runes without block discount -- premium 198 G\", () => {\n      const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n      const items = Array.from({ length: 7 }, () => ({\n        type: \"rune\",\n        material: \"stone\",\n        enchantment: 0,\n        cursed: false,\n      }));\n      expect(quote(customer, items, 0)).toBe(198);\n    });\n    it(\"should quote 2 runes + 1 moonstone as different types -- premium 88 G\", () => {\n      const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n      const items = [\n        { type: \"rune\", material: \"stone\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false },\n        { type: \"rune\", material: \"stone\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false },\n        { type: \"moonstone\", material: \"gem\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false },\n      ];\n      expect(quote(customer, items, 0)).toBe(88);\n    });\n    it(\"should quote 3 runes + 3 moonstones as two blocks -- premium 137 G\", () => {\n      const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n      const items = [\n        { type: \"rune\", material: \"stone\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false },\n        { type: \"rune\", material: \"stone\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false },\n        { type: \"rune\", material: \"stone\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false },\n        { type: \"moonstone\", material: \"gem\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false },\n        { type: \"moonstone\", material: \"gem\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false },\n        { type: \"moonstone\", material: \"gem\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false },\n      ];\n      expect(quote(customer, items, 0)).toBe(137);\n    });\n    it(\"should apply cursed surcharge to cursed sword -- premium 165 G final\", () => {\n      const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n      const items = [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 0, cursed: true }];\n      expect(quote(customer, items, 0)).toBe(165);\n    });\n    it(\"should apply high-enchantment surcharge at enchantment 5 -- premium 145 G\", () => {\n      const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n      const items = [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 5, cursed: false }];\n      expect(quote(customer, items, 0)).toBe(145);\n    });\n    it(\"should apply loyalty discount at exactly 2 years -- premium 95 G\", () => {\n      const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 2 };\n      const items = [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false }];\n      expect(quote(customer, items, 0)).toBe(95);\n    });\n    it(\"should apply follow-up contract discount on second contract -- premium 100 G\", () => {\n      const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n      const items = [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false }];\n      expect(quote(customer, items, 1)).toBe(100);\n    });\n    it(\"should handle newcomer with cursed sword -- premium 165 G\", () => {\n      const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n      const items = [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: true }];\n      expect(quote(customer, items, 0)).toBe(165);\n    });\n    it(\"should handle long-standing customer second contract with cursed enchanted sword -- premium 160 G\", () => {\n      const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 3 };\n      const items = [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 7, cursed: true }];\n      expect(quote(customer, items, 1)).toBe(160);\n    });\n    it.todo(\"should sum insurance values for multiple items of same type -- two swords sum 2000 G\");\n    it.todo(\"should quote a mixed policy with item-specific and policy-wide modifiers\");\n    it.todo(\"should reject unknown item type in quote\");\n  });\n\n  describe(\"claim\", () => {\n    it.todo(\"should pay regular sword damage 500 G minus deductible -- payout 400 G\");\n    it.todo(\"should pay rune damage 200 G minus deductible -- payout 100 G\");\n    it.todo(\"should apply high-enchantment clause to dragon-material sword enchantment 8 -- payout 400 G\");\n    it.todo(\"should apply dragon-material clause to enchantment 5 sword -- payout 700 G\");\n    it.todo(\"should apply high-enchantment clause to steel sword enchantment 9 -- payout 400 G\");\n    it.todo(\"should apply high-enchantment clause over dragon material when both apply -- payout 400 G\");\n    it.todo(\"should apply deductible per damaged item in multi-item incident\");\n    it.todo(\"should cap total payout at twice the insurance sum\");\n    it.todo(\"should exhaust cap across successive claims\");\n    it.todo(\"should reject claim for item not in policy\");\n    it.todo(\"should reject claim with negative damage amount\");\n    it.todo(\"should reject claim with more damages of a type than policy covers\");\n  });\n\n  describe(\"processScenario\", () => {\n    it.todo(\"should process quote then claim from schema example\");\n  });\n});\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784970557089},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"We have src/claim-office.ts with quote, claim, processScenario. Tests only for quote currently implemented (17 passing). We need to refactor. Need to evaluate naming, apply simple design rules, calcul