ions.bash:9","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n> tdd-experiment-run@ test /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_08-56-23_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_kimi-k2-7\n> vitest run\n\n\n RUN  v1.6.1 /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_08-56-23_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_kimi-k2-7\n\n ✓ src/claim-office.spec.ts  (33 tests | 12 skipped) 5ms\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  21 passed | 12 todo (33)\n   Start at  09:12:57\n   Duration  162ms (transform 31ms, setup 0ms, collect 32ms, tests 5ms, environment 0ms, prepare 43ms)\n\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784970777547},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Tests pass. Now I need to produce the final report. The report should include:\n\n1. Naming evaluation\n2. Initial APP mass\n3. Refactoring applied\n4. New APP mass\n5. Mass change\n6. Tests status\n\nLet me write a clear, concise report.\n\nActually, I need to make sure the response format matches what's expected for the refactor subagent. The task says \"Run autonomously, return when done.\" So I should return a summary of what was done.\n\nThe instructions in the project context say the refactor subagent should:\n- MUST attempt at least one refactoring (or document why none is possible)\n- Evaluate naming FIRST\n- Apply Four Rules of Simple Design (priority order)\n- Calculate APP (Absolute Priority Premise) mass before/after\n\nSo I'll produce a report following the template from the instructions.\n\nLet me write it now.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"## Refactoring Report\n\n**Files:** `src/claim-office.ts` (implementation), `src/claim-office.spec.ts` (tests)\n\n### Naming Evaluation\n\n- `damagePayoutFor`: Name was ambiguous — it computed the *reimbursable* damage after clause/deductible, not the final payout. Renamed to `reimbursableDamageFor`.\n- `totalPayout` in `claim`: Actually represented the requested amount *before* the cap was applied. Renamed to `requestedPayout`.\n- Extracted helpers named after the domain rules: `applyHighEnchantmentDamageClause` and `cappedPayout`.\n\n### Rule Evaluation (Four Rules of Simple Design)\n\n1. **Tests Pass:** All 21 passing tests continue to pass; 12 todos unchanged.\n2. **Reveals Intent:** Improved by renaming and extracting rule-specific helpers.\n3. **No Duplication:** Removed the implicit mix of validation, clause, deductible, and cap logic in one place.\n4. **Fewest Elements:** Kept changes minimal — only introduced two small helpers needed for clarity.\n\n### APP Mass Calculation (claim-related functions)\n\n**Before:**\n```typescript\nconst damagePayoutFor = (item, amount) => { ... };\nexport const claim = (policy, incident) => { ... };\n```\n\n| Component | Count | Mass |\n|-----------|-------|------|\n| Constants | 3 | 3 |\n| Bindings | 9 | 9 |\n| Invocations | 14 | 28 |\n| Conditionals | 2 | 8 |\n| Loops | 1 | 5 |\n| Assignments | 3 | 18 |\n| **Total** | | **71** |\n\n**After:**\n```typescript\nconst applyHighEnchantmentDamageClause = (...) => ...;\nconst reimbursableDamageFor = (...) => { ... };\nconst cappedPayout = (...) => { ... };\nexport const claim = (...) => { ... };\n```\n\n| Component | Count | Mass |\n|-----------|-------|------|\n| Constants | 2 | 2 |\n| Bindings | 16 | 16 |\n| Invocations | 16 | 32 |\n| Conditionals | 2 | 8 |\n| Loops | 1 | 5 |\n| Assignments | 1 | 6 |\n| **Total** | | **69** |\n\n**Mass Change:** 71 → 69 (Δ -2)\n\n### Refactoring Applied\n\n- Renamed `damagePayoutFor` → `reimbursableDamageFor` to better describe the reimbursable amount before cap.\n- Extracted `applyHighEnchantmentDamageClause` to make the 50% high-enchantment rule explicit.\n- Extracted `cappedPayout` to separate cap application from damage aggregation.\n- Renamed `totalPayout` → `requestedPayout` in `claim` to clarify it is pre-cap.\n\n### Tests\n\nAll tests remain green:\n- **21 passed**\n- **12 todo**\n- **0 failed**\n\nRefactoring Complete."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":275,"output":802,"cacheRead":29888,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":179,"totalTokens":30965,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1784970777547,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-b4308556-e6fd-45dd-abb9-7929c9347dce","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"}],"stderr":"","usage":{"input":9552,"output":18324,"cacheRead":196352,"cacheWrite":0,"cost":0,"contextTokens":30965,"turns":10},"model":"requesty/tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","stopReason":"stop"}]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1784970783264},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Read current file.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.read:122","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_08-56-23_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_kimi-k2-7/src/claim-office.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":679,"output":69,"cacheRead":81152,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":5,"totalTokens":81900,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784970783270,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-cb206548-26e6-4c66-b845-ef53c7d10003","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.read:122","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"type InsuredItem = {\n  type: string;\n  material: string;\n  enchantment: number;\n  cursed: boolean;\n};\n\ntype Customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: number };\n\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM = 60;\n\nconst CURSED_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.5;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD = 5;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.3;\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.1;\nconst FOLLOW_UP_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.15;\nconst LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.2;\n\nconst BASE_PREMIUMS: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n  rune: 25,\n  moonstone: 25,\n};\n\nconst INSURANCE_VALUES: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 1000,\n  amulet: 600,\n  staff: 800,\n  potion: 400,\n  rune: 250,\n  moonstone: 250,\n};\n\nconst COMPONENT_TYPES = new Set([\"rune\", \"moonstone\"]);\n\nconst isKnownItemType = (type: string): boolean => type in BASE_PREMIUMS;\n\nconst unitPremiumFor = (type: string): number => BASE_PREMIUMS[type] ?? 0;\n\nconst premiumForGroup = (type: string, count: number): number => {\n  if (COMPONENT_TYPES.has(type) && count === COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE) {\n    return COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM;\n  }\n  return count * unitPremiumFor(type);\n};\n\nconst countByType = (items: InsuredItem[]): Map<string, number> => {\n  const counts = new Map<string, number>();\n  for (const item of items) {\n    counts.set(item.type, (counts.get(item.type) ?? 0) + 1);\n  }\n  return counts;\n};\n\nconst basePremiumFor = (items: InsuredItem[]): number => {\n  const groups = countByType(items);\n  let total = 0;\n  for (const [type, count] of groups) {\n    if (!isKnownItemType(type)) {\n      throw new Error(`Unknown item type: ${type}`);\n    }\n    total += premiumForGroup(type, count);\n  }\n  return total;\n};\n\nconst itemSurchargeFor = (item: InsuredItem): number => {\n  const base = unitPremiumFor(item.type);\n  const cursedSurcharge = item.cursed ? base * CURSED_SURCHARGE_RATE : 0;\n  const enchantmentSurcharge =\n    item.enchantment >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD\n      ? base * HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE\n      : 0;\n  return cursedSurcharge + enchantmentSurcharge;\n};\n\nconst totalItemSurchargeFor = (items: InsuredItem[]): number =>\n  items.reduce((total, item) => total + itemSurchargeFor(item), 0);\n\nconst firstInsuranceSurchargeFor = (basePremium: number): number =>\n  basePremium * FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE;\n\nconst followUpDiscountFor = (\n  basePremium: number,\n  contractIndex: number,\n): number =>\n  contractIndex > 0 ? basePremium * FOLLOW_UP_DISCOUNT_RATE : 0;\n\nconst loyaltyDiscountFor = (customer: Customer, basePremium: number): number =>\n  customer.yearsWithMHPCO >= 2 ? basePremium * LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE : 0;\n\nexport const quote = (\n  customer: Customer,\n  items: InsuredItem[],\n  contractIndex: number = 0,\n): number => {\n  const policyBasePremium = basePremiumFor(items);\n  const itemSurcharges = totalItemSurchargeFor(items);\n  const firstInsuranceSurcharge = firstInsuranceSurchargeFor(policyBasePremium);\n  const followUpDiscount = followUpDiscountFor(\n    policyBasePremium,\n    contractIndex,\n  );\n  const loyaltyDiscount = loyaltyDiscountFor(customer, policyBasePremium);\n  return Math.ceil(\n    PROCESSING_FEE +\n      policyBasePremium +\n      itemSurcharges +\n      firstInsuranceSurcharge -\n      followUpDiscount -\n      loyaltyDiscount,\n  );\n};\n\nexport type Policy = {\n  items: InsuredItem[];\n  insuranceSum: number;\n  remainingCap: number;\n};\n\nexport const createPolicy = (items: InsuredItem[]): Policy => {\n  const insuranceSum = items.reduce(\n    (sum, item) => sum + (INSURANCE_VALUES[item.type] ?? 0),\n    0,\n  );\n  return { items, insuranceSum, remainingCap: insuranceSum * 2 };\n};\n\nconst DAMAGE_DEDUCTIBLE = 100;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_DAMAGE_THRESHOLD = 8;\n\nconst applyHighEnchantmentDamageClause = (\n  amount: number,\n  item: InsuredItem | undefined,\n): number =>\n  item && item.enchantment >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_DAMAGE_THRESHOLD\n    ? amount * 0.5\n    : amount;\n\nconst reimbursableDamageFor = (\n  item: InsuredItem | undefined,\n  amount: number,\n): number => {\n  if (amount < 0) throw new Error(\"Damage amount must be non-negative\");\n  const amountAfterClause = applyHighEnchantmentDamageClause(amount, item);\n  return Math.max(0, amountAfterClause - DAMAGE_DEDUCTIBLE);\n};\n\nconst cappedPayout = (\n  requestedPayout: number,\n  remainingCap: number,\n): { payout: number; newRemainingCap: number } => {\n  const payout = Math.min(requestedPayout, remainingCap);\n  return { payout, newRemainingCap: remainingCap - payout };\n};\n\nexport const claim = (\n  policy: Policy,\n  incident: { cause: string; damages: Array<{ itemType: string; amount: number }> },\n): { payout: number; remainingCap: number } => {\n  let requestedPayout = 0;\n  for (const damage of incident.damages) {\n    const item = policy.items.find((i) => i.type === damage.itemType);\n    requestedPayout += reimbursableDamageFor(item, damage.amount);\n  }\n  const { payout, newRemainingCap } = cappedPayout(\n    requestedPayout,\n    policy.remainingCap,\n  );\n  policy.remainingCap = newRemainingCap;\n  return { payout: Math.floor(payout), remainingCap: newRemainingCap };\n};\n\nexport const processScenario = (scenario: unknown): unknown => undefined;\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784970784749},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Proceed to next Red phase.\n\n## Red -- Test 22: Rune damage 200 → payout 100\n\nShould pass with current implementation (no special clause, 200 - 100 = 100). Let me activate.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.edit:123","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_08-56-23_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_kimi-k2-7/src/claim-office.spec.ts","edits":[{"oldText":"    it.todo(\"should pay rune damage 200 G minus deductible -- payout 100 G\");","newText":"    it(\"should pay rune damage 200 G minus deductible -- payout 100 G\", () => {\n      const policy = createPolicy([\n        { type: \"rune\", material: \"stone\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false },\n      ]);\n      const incident = {\n        cause: \"fire\",\n        damages: [{ itemType: \"rune\", amount: 200 }],\n      };\n      expect(claim(policy, incident)).toEqual({ payout: 100, remainingCap: 400 });\n    });