,{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.bash:132","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n> tdd-experiment-run@ test /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_08-56-23_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_kimi-k2-7\n> vitest run\n\n\n RUN  v1.6.1 /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_08-56-23_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_kimi-k2-7\n\n ✓ src/claim-office.spec.ts  (33 tests | 7 skipped) 5ms\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  26 passed | 7 todo (33)\n   Start at  09:13:40\n   Duration  177ms (transform 37ms, setup 0ms, collect 37ms, tests 5ms, environment 0ms, prepare 45ms)\n\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784970820685},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Already passes.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.subagent:133","name":"subagent","arguments":{"agent":"refactor","agentScope":"both","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 26\nRecent Green phase: (no recent green; claim tests for high-enchantment and dragon-material all passed with existing implementation)\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Consider explicitly modeling the dragon-material reimbursement clause and the priority rule between clauses.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":273,"output":123,"cacheRead":87936,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":4,"totalTokens":88332,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784970820688,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-26b3476f-abd3-4097-9c7d-cbc01471bf0a","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.subagent:133","toolName":"subagent","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Refactoring complete. All 26 tests remain green (7 todo).\n\n## Refactoring Report\n\n### Naming Evaluation (Rule 2 — first priority)\n\n- `applyHighEnchantmentDamageClause(amount, item)` mixed predicate logic with the transformation.\n- No named concept existed for the dragon-material reimbursement clause or the priority rule.\n- **Decision:** Extract domain predicates (`isHighEnchantment`, `isDragonMaterial`), give each clause its own function (`applyHighEnchantmentDamageClause`, `applyDragonMaterialDamageClause`), and introduce `applyDamageClausesWithPriority` so the priority rule is explicit in code.\n\n### Initial APP Mass (claim damage-clause code)\n\n```ts\nconst DAMAGE_DEDUCTIBLE = 100;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_DAMAGE_THRESHOLD = 8;\n\nconst applyHighEnchantmentDamageClause = (\n  amount: number,\n  item: InsuredItem | undefined,\n): number =>\n  item && item.enchantment >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_DAMAGE_THRESHOLD\n    ? amount * 0.5\n    : amount;\n\nconst reimbursableDamageFor = (\n  item: InsuredItem | undefined,\n  amount: number,\n): number => {\n  if (amount < 0) throw new Error(\"Damage amount must be non-negative\");\n  const amountAfterClause = applyHighEnchantmentDamageClause(amount, item);\n  return Math.max(0, amountAfterClause - DAMAGE_DEDUCTIBLE);\n};\n```\n\n| Component    | Count | Mass |\n|--------------|-------|------|\n| Constants    | 5     | 5    |\n| Bindings     | 7     | 7    |\n| Invocations  | 3     | 6    |\n| Conditionals | 2     | 8    |\n| Loops        | 0     | 0    |\n| Assignments  | 0     | 0    |\n| **Total**    |       | **26** |\n\n### Refactoring Applied\n\n- Extracted `isHighEnchantment` and `isDragonMaterial` predicates.\n- Added explicit `applyDragonMaterialDamageClause` (currently identity — it represents that dragon-material items receive no additional pre-deductible reduction under current rules).\n- Added `applyDamageClausesWithPriority` to make the high-enchantment-over-dragon-material priority rule explicit.\n- Simplified `applyHighEnchantmentDamageClause` to be a pure amount transformation.\n- Kept the universal deductible in `reimbursableDamageFor`.\n\n### New APP Mass\n\n```ts\nconst DAMAGE_DEDUCTIBLE = 100;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_DAMAGE_THRESHOLD = 8;\nconst DRAGON_MATERIAL = \"dragon\";\n\nconst isHighEnchantment = (item: InsuredItem | undefined): boolean =>\n  !!item && item.enchantment >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_DAMAGE_THRESHOLD;\n\nconst isDragonMaterial = (item: InsuredItem | undefined): boolean =>\n  !!item && item.material === DRAGON_MATERIAL;\n\nconst applyHighEnchantmentDamageClause = (amount: number): number =>\n  amount * 0.5;\n\nconst applyDragonMaterialDamageClause = (amount: number): number => amount;\n\nconst applyDamageClausesWithPriority = (\n  amount: number,\n  item: InsuredItem | undefined,\n): number => {\n  if (isHighEnchantment(item)) {\n    return applyHighEnchantmentDamageClause(amount);\n  }\n  if (isDragonMaterial(item)) {\n    return applyDragonMaterialDamageClause(amount);\n  }\n  return amount;\n};\n\nconst reimbursableDamageFor = (\n  item: InsuredItem | undefined,\n  amount: number,\n): number => {\n  if (amount < 0) throw new Error(\"Damage amount must be non-negative\");\n  const amountAfterClauses = applyDamageClausesWithPriority(amount, item);\n  return Math.max(0, amountAfterClauses - DAMAGE_DEDUCTIBLE);\n};\n```\n\n| Component    | Count | Mass |\n|--------------|-------|------|\n| Constants    | 6     | 6    |\n| Bindings     | 12    | 12   |\n| Invocations  | 7     | 14   |\n| Conditionals | 3     | 12   |\n| Loops        | 0     | 0    |\n| Assignments  | 0     | 0    |\n| **Total**    |       | **44** |\n\n**Mass change:** 26 → 44 (Δ +18)\n\n### Simple Design Rule Evaluation\n\n1. **Tests pass** — ✓ `26 passed | 7 todo`\n2. **Reveals intent** — ✓ The dragon-material clause and the high-enchantment-over-dragon-material priority rule are now named and explicit.\n3. **No duplication** — ✓ Deductible logic remains in one place; clause logic is not duplicated.\n4. **Fewest elements** — Mass increased, but Rule 2 (clarity) takes priority over APP.\n\n### Notes\n\n`applyDragonMaterialDamageClause` is intentionally identity for the current test set: the existing expectations show dragon-material items receiving the standard deductible with no extra pre-deductible reduction. The function is not dead code — it documents the clause as a named extension point and makes the priority rule readable."}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_08-56-23_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_kimi-k2-7/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 26\nRecent Green phase: (no recent green; claim tests for high-enchantment and dragon-material all passed with existing implementation)\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Consider explicitly modeling the dragon-material reimbursement clause and the priority rule between clauses.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 26\nRecent Green phase: (no recent green; claim tests for high-enchantment and dragon-material all passed with existing implementation)\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Consider explicitly modeling the dragon-material reimbursement clause and the priority rule between clauses.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784970823493},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me start by reading the current implementation and tests to understand what we're working with.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.read:0","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_08-56-23_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_kimi-k2-7/src/claim-office.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.read:1","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_08-56-23_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_kimi-k2-7/src/claim-office.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":89,"output":144,"cacheRead":6016,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":18,"totalTokens":6249,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784970823514,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-f20af164-29d1-4e85-a1cd-bcddffde2a2d","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.read:0","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"type InsuredItem = {\n  type: string;\n  material: string;\n  enchantment: number;\n  cursed: boolean;\n};\n\ntype Customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: number };\n\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM = 60;\n\nconst CURSED_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.5;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD = 5;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.3;\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.1;\nconst FOLLOW_UP_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.15;\nconst LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.2;\n\nconst BASE_PREMIUMS: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n  rune: 25,\n  moonstone: 25,\n};\n\nconst INSURANCE_VALUES: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 1000,\n  amulet: 600,\n  staff: 800,\n  potion: 400,\n  rune: 250,\n  moonstone: 250,\n};\n\nconst COMPONENT_TYPES = new Set([\"rune\", \"moonstone\"]);\n\nconst isKnownItemType = (type: string): boolean => type in BASE_PREMIUMS;\n\nconst unitPremiumFor = (type: string): number => BASE_PREMIUMS[type] ?? 0;\n\nconst premiumForGroup = (type: string, count: number): number => {\n  if (COMPONENT_TYPES.has(type) && count === COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE) {\n    return COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM;\n  }\n  return count * unitPremiumFor(type);\n};\n\nconst countByType = (items: InsuredItem[]): Map<string, number> => {\n  const counts = new Map<string, number>();\n  for (const item of items) {\n    counts.set(item.type, (counts.get(item.type) ?? 0) + 1);\n  }\n  return counts;\n};\n\nconst basePremiumFor = (items: InsuredItem[]): number => {\n  const groups = countByType(items);\n  let total = 0;\n  for (const [type, count] of groups) {\n    if (!isKnownItemType(type)) {\n      throw new Error(`Unknown item type: ${type}`);\n    }\n    total += premiumForGroup(type, count);\n  }\n  return total;\n};\n\nconst itemSurchargeFor = (item: InsuredItem): number => {\n  const base = unitPremiumFor(item.type);\n  const cursedSurcharge = item.cursed ? base * CURSED_SURCHARGE_RATE : 0;\n  const enchantmentSurcharge =\n    item.enchantment >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD\n      ? base * HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE\n      : 0;\n  return cursedSurcharge + enchantmentSurcharge;\n};\n\nconst totalItemSurchargeFor = (items: InsuredItem[]): number =>\n  items.reduce((total, item) => total + itemSurchargeFor(item), 0);\n\nconst firstInsuranceSurchargeFor = (basePremium: number): number =>\n  basePremium * FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE;\n\nconst followUpDiscountFor = (\n  basePremium: number,\n  contractIndex: number,\n): number =>\n  contractIndex > 0 ? basePremium * FOLLOW_UP_DISCOUNT_RATE : 0;\n\nconst loyaltyDiscountFor = (customer: Customer, basePremium: number): number =>\n  customer.yearsWithMHPCO >= 2 ? basePremium * LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE : 0;\n\nexport const quote = (\n  customer: Customer,\n  items: InsuredItem[],\n  contractIndex: number = 0,\n): number => {\n  const policyBasePremium = basePremiumFor(items);\n  const itemSurcharges = totalItemSurchargeFor(items);\n  const firstInsuranceSurcharge = firstInsuranceSurchargeFor(policyBasePremium);\n  const followUpDiscount = followUpDiscountFor(\n    policyBasePremium,\n    contractIndex,\n  );\n  const loyaltyDiscount = loyaltyDiscountFor(customer, policyBasePremium);\n  return Math.ceil(\n    PROCESSING_FEE +\n      policyBasePremium +\n      itemSurcharges +\n      firstInsuranceSurcharge -\n      followUpDiscount -\n      loyaltyDiscount,\n  );\n};\n\nexport type Policy = {\n  items: InsuredItem[];\n  insuranceSum: number;\n  remainingCap: number;\n};\n\nexport const createPolicy = (items: InsuredItem[]): Policy => {\n  const insuranceSum = items.reduce(\n    (sum, item) => sum + (INSURANCE_VALUES[item.type] ?? 0),\n    0,\n  );\n  return { items, insuranceSum, remainingCap: insuranceSum * 2 };\n};\n\nconst DAMAGE_DEDUCTIBLE = 100;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_DAMAGE_THRESHOLD = 8;\n\nconst applyHighEnchantmentDamageClause = (\n  amount: number,\n  item: InsuredItem | undefined,\n): number =>\n  item && item.enchantment >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_DAMAGE_THRESHOLD\n    ? amount * 0.5\n    : amount;\n\nconst reimbursableDamageFor = (\n  item: InsuredItem | undefined,\n  amount: number,\n): number => {\n  if (amount < 0) throw new Error(\"Damage amount must be non-negative\");\n  const amountAfterClause = applyHighEnchantmentDamageClause(amount, item);\n  return Math.max(0, amountAfterClause - DAMAGE_DEDUCTIBLE);\n};\n\nconst cappedPayout = (\n  requestedPayout: number,\n  remainingCap: number,\n): { payout: number; newRemainingCap: number } => {\n  const payout = Math.min(requestedPayout, remainingCap);\n  return { payout, newRemainingCap: remainingCap - payout };\n};\n\nexport const claim = (\n  policy: Policy,\n  incident: { cause: string; damages: Array<{ itemType: string; amount: number }> },\n): { payout: number; remainingCap: number } => {\n  let requestedPayout = 0;\n  for (const damage of incident.damages) {\n    const item = policy.items.find((i) => i.type === damage.itemType);\n    requestedPayout += reimbursableDamageFor(item, damage.amount);\n  }\n  const { payout, newRemainingCap } = cappedPayout(\n    requestedPayout,\n    policy.remainingCap,\n  );\n  policy.remainingCap = newRemainingCap;\n  return { payout: Math.floor(payout), remainingCap: newRemainingCap };\n};\n\nexport const processScenario = (scenario: unknown): unknown => undefined;\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784970824368},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.read:1","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { quote, claim, processScenario, createPolicy } from \"./claim-office.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"MHPCO Claim Office\", () => {\n  describe(\"quote\", () => {\n    it(\"should return premium 5 G for empty item list -- only processing fee\", () => {\n      const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n      expect(quote(customer, [])).toBe(5);\n    });\n    it(\"should quote a single sword -- premium 115 G\", () => {\n      const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n      const items = [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false }];\n      expect(quote(customer, items, 0)).toBe(115);\n    });\n    it(\"should quote a single amulet -- premium 71 G\", () => {\n      const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n      const items = [{ type: \"amulet\", material: \"silver\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false }];\n      expect(quote(customer, items, 0)).toBe(71);\n    });\n    it(\"should quote a single staff -- premium 93 G\", () => {\n      const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n      const items = [{ type: \"staff\", material: \"wood\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false }];\n      expect(quote(customer, items, 0)).toBe(93);\n    });\n    it(\"should quote a single potion -- premium 49 G\", () => {\n      const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n      const items = [{ type: \"potion\", material: \"glass\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false }];\n      expect(quote(customer, items, 0)).toBe(49);\n    });\n    it(\"should quote 2 runes without block discount -- premium 60 G\", () => {\n      const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n      const items = [\n        { type: \"rune\", material: \"stone\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false },\n        { type: \"rune\", material: \"stone\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false },\n      ];\n      expect(quote(customer, items, 0)).toBe(60);\n    });\n    it(\"should quote 3 runes with block discount -- premium 71 G\", () => {\n      const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n      const items = [\n        { type: \"rune\", material: \"stone\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false },\n        { type: \"rune\", material: \"stone\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false },\n        { type: \"rune\", material: \"stone\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false },\n      ];\n      expect(quote(customer, items, 0)).toBe(71);\n    });\n    it(\"should quote 4 runes without block discount -- premium 115 G\", () => {\n      const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n      const items = [\n        { type: \"rune\", material: \"stone\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false },\n        { type: \"rune\", material: \"stone\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false },\n        { type: \"rune\", material: \"stone\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false },\n        { type: \"rune\", material: \"stone\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false },\n      ];\n      expect(quote(customer, items, 0)).toBe(115);\n    });\n    it(\"should quote 7 runes without block discount -- premium 198 G\", () => {\n      const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n      const items = Array.from({ length: 7 }, () => ({\n        type: \"rune\",\n        material: \"stone\",\n        enchantment: 0,\n        cursed: false,\n      }));\n      expect(quote(customer, items, 0)).toBe(198);\n    });\n    it(\"should quote 2 runes + 1 moonstone as different types -- premium 88 G\", () => {\n      const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n      const items = [\n        { type: \"rune\", material: \"stone\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false },\n        { type: \"rune\", material: \"stone\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false },\n        { type: \"moonstone\", material: \"gem\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false },\n      ];\n      expect(quote(customer, items, 0)).toBe(88);\n    });\n    it(\"should quote 3 runes + 3 moonstones as two blocks -- premium 137 G\", () => {\n      const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n      const items = [\n        { type: \"rune\", material: \"stone\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false },\n        { type: \"rune\", material: \"stone\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false },\n        { type: \"rune\", material: \"stone\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false },\n        { type: \"moonstone\", material: \"gem\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false },\n        { type: \"moonstone\", material: \"gem\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false },\n        { type: \"moonstone\", material: \"gem\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false },\n      ];\n      expect(quote(customer, items, 0)).toBe(137);\n    });\n    it(\"should apply cursed surcharge to cursed sword -- premium 165 G final\", () => {\n      const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n      const items = [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 0, cursed: true }];\n      expect(quote(customer, items, 0)).toBe(165);\n    });\n    it(\"should apply high-enchantment surcharge at enchantment 5 -- premium 145 G\", () => {\n      const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n      const items = [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 5, cursed: false }];\n      expect(quote(customer, items, 0)).toBe(145);\n    });\n    it(\"should apply loyalty discount at exactly 2 years -- premium 95 G\", () => {\n      const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 2 };\n      const items = [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false }];\n      expect(quote(customer, items, 0)).toBe(95);\n    });\n    it(\"should apply follow-up contract discount on second contract -- premium 100 G\", () => {\n      const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n      const items = [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false }];\n      expect(quote(customer, items, 1)).toBe(100);\n    });\n    it(\"should handle newcomer with cursed sword -- premium 165 G\", () => {\n      const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n      const items = [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: true }];\n      expect(quote(customer, items, 0)).toBe(165);\n    });\n    it(\"should handle long-standing customer second contract with cursed enchanted sword -- premium 160 G\", () => {\n      const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 3 };\n      const items = [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 7, cursed: true }];\n      expect(quote(customer, items, 1)).toBe(160);\n    });\n    it(\"should quote two swords -- premium 225 G\", () => {\n      const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n      const items = [\n        { type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false },\n        { type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false },\n      ];\n      expect(quote(customer, items, 0)).toBe(225);\n    });\n    it(\"should quote a mixed policy with item-specific and policy-wide modifiers -- premium 231 G\", () => {\n      const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n      const items = [\n        { type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 0, cursed: true },\n        { type: \"amulet\", material: \"silver\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false },\n      ];\n      expect(quote(customer, items, 0)).toBe(231);\n    });\n    it(\"should reject unknown item type in quote\", () => {\n      const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n      const items = [{ type: \"broomstick\", material: \"wood\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false }];\n      expect(() => quote(customer, items, 0)).toThrow(\"Unknown item type\");\n    });\n  });\n\n  describe(\"claim\", () => {\n    it(\"should pay regular sword damage 500 G minus deductible -- payout 400 G\", () => {\n      const policy = createPolicy([\n        { type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: false },\n      ]);\n      const incident = {\n        cause: \"fire\",\n        damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 500 }],\n      };\n      expect(claim(policy, incident)).toEqual({ payout: 400, remainingCap: 1600 });\n    });\n    it(\"should pay rune damage 200 G minus deductible -- payout 100 G\", () => {\n      const policy = createPolicy([\n        { type: \"rune\", material: \"stone\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false },\n      ]);\n      const incident = {\n        cause: \"fire\",\n        damages: [{ itemType: \"rune\", amount: 200 }],\n      };\n      expect(claim(policy, incident)).toEqual({ payout: 100, remainingCap: 400 });\n    });\n    it(\"should apply high-enchantment clause to dragon-material sword enchantment 8 -- payout 400 G\", () => {\n      const policy = createPolicy([\n        { type: \"sword\", material: \"dragon\", enchantment: 8, cursed: false },\n      ]);\n      const incident = {\n        cause: \"fire\",\n        damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 1000 }],\n      };\n      expect(claim(policy, incident)).toEqual({ payout: 400, remainingCap: 1600 });\n    });\n    it(\"should apply dragon-material clause to enchantment 5 sword -- payout 700 G\", () => {\n      const policy = createPolicy([\n        { type: \"sword\", material: \"dragon\", enchantment: 5, cursed: false },\n      ]);\n      const incident = {\n        cause: \"fire\",\n        damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 800 }],\n      };\n      expect(claim(policy, incident)).toEqual({ payout: 700, remainingCap: 1300 });\n    });\n    it(\"should apply high-enchantment clause to steel sword enchantment 9 -- payout 400 G\", () => {\n      const policy = createPolicy([\n        { type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 9, cursed: false },\n      ]);\n      const incident = {\n        cause: \"fire\",\n        damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 1000 }],\n      };\n      expect(claim(policy, incident)).toEqual({ payout: 400, remainingCap: 1600 });\n    });\n    it(\"should apply high-enchantment clause over dragon material when both apply -- payout 400 G\", () => {\n      const policy = createPolicy([\n        { type: \"sword\", material: \"dragon\", enchantment: 9, cursed: false },\n      ]);\n      const incident = {\n        cause: \"fire\",\n        damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 1000 }],\n      };\n      expect(claim(policy, incident)).toEqual({ payout: 400, remainingCap: 1600 });\n    });\n    it.todo(\"should apply deductible per damaged item in multi-item incident\");\n    it.todo(\"should cap total payout at twice the insurance sum\");\n    it.todo(\"should exhaust cap across successive claims\");\n    it.todo(\"should reject claim for item not in policy\");\n    it.todo(\"should reject claim with negative damage amount\");\n    it.todo(\"should reject claim with more damages of a type than policy covers\");\n  });\n\n  describe(\"processScenario\", () => {\n    it.todo(\"should process quote then claim from schema example\");\n  });\n});\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784970824369},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me understand the code and tests. The claim function has these tests that pass:\n1. Regular sword damage 500 - deductible 100 = 400\n2. Rune damage 200 - deductible 100 = 100\n3. High-enchantment clause for dragon-material sword enchantment 8: amount 1000 -> 50% -> 500 -> -100 = 400\n4. Dragon-material clause for enchantment 5: amount 800 -> ? -> 700\n5. High-enchantment for steel enchantment 9: 1000 -> 50% -> 500 -> -100 = 400\n6. High-enchantment priority over dragon material when both apply: 1000 -> 50% -> 500 -> -100 = 400\n\nWait, looking at the current implementation, there's only `applyHighEnchantmentDamageClause`. The dragon-material clause isn't explicitly modeled. Let me check how test 4 passes:\n- Dragon material, enchantment 5, amount 800 -> payout 700\n- With current code: enchantment 5 < 8, so high-enchantment doesn't apply. Then 800 - 100 = 700. So it passes because no clause applies except deductible.\n- But the test says \"should apply dragon-material cla