ops: 6\n- Assignments: 3\n- Total: 329\n- Mass change: 363 -> 329 (−34)\n\nWait after loyalty threshold we have bindings 91. Yes.\n\n**Rule evaluation**:\n- Rule 1 tests pass: 29 passing, 4 todo.\n- Rule 2 reveals intent: names improved, comment added.\n- Rule 3 no duplication: removed duplicate INSURANCE_VALUES map; removed no-op dragon branch.\n- Rule 4 fewest elements: removed 2 helpers, 1 map, 1 constant; used derived helper.\n\n**Refactoring applied** list.\n\nNeed mention lint also passes (no eslint errors). Type check passes.\n\nPotential subtlety: Our AST counter counts `const` declarations as bindings; the `INSURANCE_VALUE_MULTIPLIER = 10` etc. We should mention method used. The user may not care. But instructions require documentation.\n\nWe should also mention that we deleted temporary mass scripts.\n\nShould we mention processScenario unchanged because no tests? Yes.\n\nNow final answer. Ensure we don't add extraneous. Use markdown sections.\n\nOne thing: the instructions say \"Return the report to the requester.\" We are subagent. We should output final report only.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"**Refactoring Complete**\n\n### Naming Evaluation (Rule 2 – first priority)\n\n| Current name | Purpose | Assessment | Decision |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `unitPremiumFor` | Looks up the base premium for a single item type | Too generic; does not say it is a per-type base-premium lookup | **Rename to `basePremiumForType`** |\n| `INSURANCE_VALUES` map | Stores insurance values that are always 10 × the base premium | Duplicates knowledge already in `BASE_PREMIUMS` | **Remove map; derive with `insuranceValueForType`** |\n| `applyDragonMaterialDamageClause` | Returned the amount unchanged | No-op helper that added elements without behavior | **Remove and document intent with a comment** |\n| Magic `2` in `createPolicy` and `loyaltyDiscountFor` | Cap multiplier / loyalty-year threshold | Raw literals hide meaning | **Name as `CAP_MULTIPLIER` and `LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD`** |\n\n### APP Mass Calculation\n\nI used an AST-based counter that categorizes TypeScript nodes as constants, bindings, invocations, conditionals, loops, and assignments, with the APP weights.\n\n**Before refactoring:**\n\n```\nConstants:    50\nBindings:     95\nInvocations:  67\nConditionals:  9\nLoops:         6\nAssignments:   3\nTotal Mass:  363\n```\n\n**After refactoring:**\n\n```\nConstants:    40\nBindings:     91\nInvocations:  59\nConditionals:  8\nLoops:         6\nAssignments:   3\nTotal Mass:  329\n```\n\n**Mass change:** `363 → 329` (−34)\n\n### Simple Design Rules Applied\n\n1. **Tests pass** — `pnpm test` passes: 29 tests green, 4 still todo.\n2. **Reveals intent** — `basePremiumForType`, `insuranceValueForType`, `CAP_MULTIPLIER`, `LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD`, and the dragon-material comment all make the rules explicit.\n3. **No duplication** — removed the `INSURANCE_VALUES` map (values derived from base premiums); removed the no-op dragon-material branch and identity helper.\n4. **Fewest elements** — dropped `INSURANCE_VALUES`, `DRAGON_MATERIAL`, `isDragonMaterial`, and `applyDragonMaterialDamageClause`.\n\n### Refactorings Applied\n\n- Renamed `unitPremiumFor` → `basePremiumForType`.\n- Added `insuranceValueForType` and `INSURANCE_VALUE_MULTIPLIER`; removed the `INSURANCE_VALUES` lookup table.\n- Added `CAP_MULTIPLIER` for the policy cap.\n- Simplified damage-clause handling by removing the identity dragon-material branch; high-enchantment reduction is now explicit, with a comment noting that dragon material is reimbursed in full.\n- Added `LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD` and made `loyaltyDiscountFor` use it.\n- `processScenario` left unchanged because no tests drive it yet.\n\n### Verification\n\n- `pnpm test` — 29 passing, 4 todo.\n- `npx tsc --noEmit` — no type errors.\n- `npx eslint src/claim-office.ts` — no lint errors."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":22,"output":1249,"cacheRead":31808,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":558,"totalTokens":33079,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1784971052128,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-3074b3ae-2097-47c3-87fb-0ed5b779b2cb","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"}],"stderr":"","usage":{"input":11910,"output":15633,"cacheRead":375680,"cacheWrite":0,"cost":0,"contextTokens":33079,"turns":17},"model":"requesty/tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","stopReason":"stop"}]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1784971061006},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Read current file.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.read:142","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_08-56-23_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_kimi-k2-7/src/claim-office.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":761,"output":69,"cacheRead":93376,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":5,"totalTokens":94206,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784971061012,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-2ad5ec48-e9e5-4f68-b26f-ce5e94523d16","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.read:142","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"type InsuredItem = {\n  type: string;\n  material: string;\n  enchantment: number;\n  cursed: boolean;\n};\n\ntype Customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: number };\n\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM = 60;\n\nconst CURSED_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.5;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD = 5;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.3;\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.1;\nconst FOLLOW_UP_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.15;\nconst LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.2;\nconst LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD = 2;\n\nconst BASE_PREMIUMS: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n  rune: 25,\n  moonstone: 25,\n};\n\nconst COMPONENT_TYPES = new Set([\"rune\", \"moonstone\"]);\n\nconst INSURANCE_VALUE_MULTIPLIER = 10;\nconst CAP_MULTIPLIER = 2;\n\nconst isKnownItemType = (type: string): boolean => type in BASE_PREMIUMS;\n\nconst basePremiumForType = (type: string): number => BASE_PREMIUMS[type] ?? 0;\n\nconst insuranceValueForType = (type: string): number =>\n  basePremiumForType(type) * INSURANCE_VALUE_MULTIPLIER;\n\nconst premiumForGroup = (type: string, count: number): number => {\n  if (COMPONENT_TYPES.has(type) && count === COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE) {\n    return COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM;\n  }\n  return count * basePremiumForType(type);\n};\n\nconst countByType = (items: InsuredItem[]): Map<string, number> => {\n  const counts = new Map<string, number>();\n  for (const item of items) {\n    counts.set(item.type, (counts.get(item.type) ?? 0) + 1);\n  }\n  return counts;\n};\n\nconst basePremiumFor = (items: InsuredItem[]): number => {\n  const groups = countByType(items);\n  let total = 0;\n  for (const [type, count] of groups) {\n    if (!isKnownItemType(type)) {\n      throw new Error(`Unknown item type: ${type}`);\n    }\n    total += premiumForGroup(type, count);\n  }\n  return total;\n};\n\nconst itemSurchargeFor = (item: InsuredItem): number => {\n  const base = basePremiumForType(item.type);\n  const cursedSurcharge = item.cursed ? base * CURSED_SURCHARGE_RATE : 0;\n  const enchantmentSurcharge =\n    item.enchantment >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD\n      ? base * HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE\n      : 0;\n  return cursedSurcharge + enchantmentSurcharge;\n};\n\nconst totalItemSurchargeFor = (items: InsuredItem[]): number =>\n  items.reduce((total, item) => total + itemSurchargeFor(item), 0);\n\nconst firstInsuranceSurchargeFor = (basePremium: number): number =>\n  basePremium * FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE;\n\nconst followUpDiscountFor = (\n  basePremium: number,\n  contractIndex: number,\n): number =>\n  contractIndex > 0 ? basePremium * FOLLOW_UP_DISCOUNT_RATE : 0;\n\nconst loyaltyDiscountFor = (customer: Customer, basePremium: number): number =>\n  customer.yearsWithMHPCO >= LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD\n    ? basePremium * LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE\n    : 0;\n\nexport const quote = (\n  customer: Customer,\n  items: InsuredItem[],\n  contractIndex: number = 0,\n): number => {\n  const policyBasePremium = basePremiumFor(items);\n  const itemSurcharges = totalItemSurchargeFor(items);\n  const firstInsuranceSurcharge = firstInsuranceSurchargeFor(policyBasePremium);\n  const followUpDiscount = followUpDiscountFor(\n    policyBasePremium,\n    contractIndex,\n  );\n  const loyaltyDiscount = loyaltyDiscountFor(customer, policyBasePremium);\n  return Math.ceil(\n    PROCESSING_FEE +\n      policyBasePremium +\n      itemSurcharges +\n      firstInsuranceSurcharge -\n      followUpDiscount -\n      loyaltyDiscount,\n  );\n};\n\nexport type Policy = {\n  items: InsuredItem[];\n  insuranceSum: number;\n  remainingCap: number;\n};\n\nexport const createPolicy = (items: InsuredItem[]): Policy => {\n  const insuranceSum = items.reduce(\n    (sum, item) => sum + insuranceValueForType(item.type),\n    0,\n  );\n  return { items, insuranceSum, remainingCap: insuranceSum * CAP_MULTIPLIER };\n};\n\nconst DAMAGE_DEDUCTIBLE = 100;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_DAMAGE_THRESHOLD = 8;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_DAMAGE_MULTIPLIER = 0.5;\n\nconst applyDamageClausesWithPriority = (\n  amount: number,\n  item?: InsuredItem,\n): number => {\n  if (item && item.enchantment >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_DAMAGE_THRESHOLD) {\n    return amount * HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_DAMAGE_MULTIPLIER;\n  }\n  // Dragon-material items are reimbursed in full, so no reduction applies.\n  return amount;\n};\n\nconst reimbursableDamageFor = (\n  item: InsuredItem | undefined,\n  amount: number,\n): number => {\n  if (amount < 0) throw new Error(\"Damage amount must be non-negative\");\n  const amountAfterClauses = applyDamageClausesWithPriority(amount, item);\n  return Math.max(0, amountAfterClauses - DAMAGE_DEDUCTIBLE);\n};\n\nconst cappedPayout = (\n  requestedPayout: number,\n  remainingCap: number,\n): { payout: number; newRemainingCap: number } => {\n  const payout = Math.min(requestedPayout, remainingCap);\n  return { payout, newRemainingCap: remainingCap - payout };\n};\n\nexport const claim = (\n  policy: Policy,\n  incident: { cause: string; damages: Array<{ itemType: string; amount: number }> },\n): { payout: number; remainingCap: number } => {\n  let requestedPayout = 0;\n  for (const damage of incident.damages) {\n    const item = policy.items.find((i) => i.type === damage.itemType);\n    requestedPayout += reimbursableDamageFor(item, damage.amount);\n  }\n  const { payout, newRemainingCap } = cappedPayout(\n    requestedPayout,\n    policy.remainingCap,\n  );\n  policy.remainingCap = newRemainingCap;\n  return { payout: Math.floor(payout), remainingCap: newRemainingCap };\n};\n\nexport const processScenario = (scenario: unknown): unknown => undefined;\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784971062578},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Wait, the refactor removed the dragon material clause explicit handling. But the spec example says dragon material enchantment 5 sword damage 800 → payout 700. Without explicit dragon material, the default full reimbursement gives 700. So tests still pass. But the spec rule is not explicitly implemented. However, the comment says dragon material is reimbursed in full.\n\nActually, the current implementation: if enchantment >= 8, apply 50%. Otherwise, full reimbursement (which covers dragon material and regular items). This matches the spec because dragon material gets full reimbursement by default, and high enchantment overrides even for dragon material. So it's correct.\n\nBut wait, the spec says \"Damage to items made of dragon material is fully reimbursed.\" Is there any case where a non-dragon item would NOT be fully reimbursed? Only if high enchantment applies. So the default is full reimbursement. The dragon material rule is redundant with default behavior, except it confirms that dragon material gets full reimbursement even if other clauses would reduce it. But the only reducing clause is high enchantment, which explicitly wins over dragon material. So the implementation is correct.\n\nOK, proceed. Next tests are error handling.\n\n## Red -- Test 30: Reject claim for item not in policy\n\nClaim for amulet when only sword insured. Should throw error.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.edit:143","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_08-56-23_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_kimi-k2-7/src/claim-office.spec.ts","edits":[{"oldText":"    it.todo(\"should reject claim for item not in policy\");","newText":"    it(\"should reject claim for item not in policy\", () => {\n      const policy = createPolicy([\n        { type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: false },\n      ]);\n      const incident = {\n        cause: \"fire\",\n        damages: [{ itemType: \"amulet\", amount: 200 }],\n      };\n      expect(() => claim(policy, incident)).toThrow(\"not part of the policy\");\n    });"}]}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":1539,"output":474,"cacheRead":94144,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":266,"totalTokens":96157,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784971062587,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-f249bf0d-e3a4-4338-b3f7-a3b0d9d2f0ac","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.edit:143","toolName":"edit","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully replaced 1 block(s) in /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_08-56-23_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuat